# Documentation maintenance

When a change affects what users can see or do, update the matching source under `docs/` in the same change, then regenerate the bundle.

| Change | Update |
| --- | --- |
| UI control, label, or workflow | `docs/user-guide.md` and `docs/FAQ.md` |
| Setting, default, or job/settings JSON | `docs/configuration.md` |
| Error text or recovery | `docs/troubleshooting.md` and `docs/FAQ.md` |
| Compare/sync rules, limits, CLI | `docs/reference.md` |
| Install or data locations | `docs/getting-started.md` |
| Shipped vs not shipped | `docs/roadmap.md` and `docs/product.md` |
| Build or docs commands | `docs/development.md` |

Then run `npm run docs:build` and commit `AI-SUPPORT.md` with the source edits.

Do not hand-edit `AI-SUPPORT.md`. `npm run docs:check` must pass.

Do not document controls that are not in the UI. Schema-only fields stay in the roadmap as not a finished feature.

Engineering docs (`ARCHITECTURE.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, and the rest of the existing set) stay; do not delete them to “replace” them with the support articles.
